<h3>Three concepts</h3>
<ul>
    <li><strong>What Claude Code is</strong> — a CLI tool that lets you hand coding work to Claude from a terminal or an IDE. It reads and edits files, runs commands, and helps you develop.</li>
    <li><strong>What a plugin is</strong> — an extension pack that adds new features to Claude Code. Install it once and dedicated commands and behaviors are added.</li>
    <li><strong>What OMC adds</strong> — it lets you use advanced ways of working such as "implement it all the way through on its own", "several workers split the job", and "verify automatically after the work" with a single command.</li>
</ul>

<p>This document is a summary written by installing it directly in a local environment for <strong>partial verification</strong> and by cross-checking the official documentation, release notes, and plugin documentation. Some commands and behaviors may differ depending on <strong>Windows PowerShell, WSL2, macOS, or Linux</strong>, so environment-dependent items are marked separately. The reference version is <strong>v4.15.2</strong> (checked 2026-07-05). Since releases are fairly frequent at 3–5 per month, the details may differ from the latest release notes at the time you read this.</p>

